{"body":"Found downstream, in MediaIngredientMech, while reviving a consumer of `mappings/kgmicrobe_unified_entity_mappings.sssom.tsv.gz` that had been dead for four months (CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech#578).\n\n`kgm.name:*` rows index a handful of MediaDive recipe annotations as if they were names of the chemical:\n\n```\nCHEBI:26710   '(adjust if required in range 100-150)'\nCHEBI:26710   '(for Agar medium autoclave separately)'\nCHEBI:2509    '(for solid medium)'\nCHEBI:2509    '(for solid medium, alternative)'\nCHEBI:2511    '(for solid medium, alternative)'\nCHEBI:26833   '(sterilized by steaming for 3 hours on 3 consecutive days)'\nCHEBI:29377   '(adjust if required)'\nCHEBI:32145   '(adjust if required)'\nCHEBI:3311    '(if required)'\nCHEBI:34545   'NaNO3(autoclave before adding)(Fisher BP360-500)'\nCHEBI:17020   'autoclaved, Glucomannan (konjac)'\nCHEBI:28087   'autoclaved, Glycogen'\nCHEBI:62969   'autoclaved'\nCHEBI:62969   'autoclaved, polygalacturonic acid'\nCHEBI:201433  'not filter sterilized'\n```\n\nThese read as fragments of a recipe's preparation instructions that were split on the ingredient boundary and kept as separate names. `'autoclaved'` under `CHEBI:62969` is the clearest: a preparation state, indexed as a name of polygalacturonic acid.\n\n**Scale: 15 forms across 12 entities, out of 257,533 surface forms carried on entities.** Tiny, and no downstream consumer is broken by it — MIM's P4.4 rule surfaces them as synonym *candidates* that a human must accept, so nothing lands automatically.\n\nFiled here rather than fixed downstream because no lexical rule separates them safely. The obvious one — drop wholly-parenthesised forms — matches **709** forms of which only 9 are these, a precision of 1.3%, because IUPAC names routinely open with a stereodescriptor and close with charge notation:\n\n```\n(8Z,11Z,14Z)-5,6-epoxyicosatrienoyl-CoA(4-)\n(3R,7S)-12-OH-JA-Ile(1-)\n(m-CPP)\n```\n\nThe distinction is semantic, not syntactic, so it needs the MediaDive provenance that is still visible where the name index is built and gone by the time a consumer reads the published set.\n\nNot urgent. Filed so the noise is on the record before a curator meets it and concludes the cross-reference is broken.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01DvFHNFmJfmh6kQFRumKdUJ","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOEqLYd88AAAABXC6W9g","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Merged #1152/#1156 protect all 15 original instruction/name-target assertions plus the 25-case regression cohort, including equivalent embedded CAS namespaces. The final conservative candidate contains zero active rejected instruction identities/unsafe labels and preserves the original rejected rows in quarantine; repeated generation is byte-identical. Keep this artifact issue open until supported/unified production promotion and fresh source/merge verification under #1123. The existing production artifact was not silently overwritten.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T00:29:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1009#issuecomment-5841524470","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOEqLYd88AAAABXOaa5g","author":{"login":"realmarcin"},"authorAssociation":"MEMBER","body":"Closing the finite recipe-instruction identity defect after production mapping\npromotion, rebuilt source/archive verification, and independent review.\n#1152/#1156 supplied the target-scoped guards; #1172 promoted the reviewed pair.\n\n- All **15 original pairs / 12 entities** and the expanded **25-case** recipe\n  cohort are covered. The promoted unified mapping is SHA256\n  `9e481e31f23b7a2414537f967ea513a7b494824799a002ca4300765f5acea0f1`;\n  supported MIM input is\n  `6b52b30e018b369aa322d41dfd4e81fcfae0e895e34d7fe48900abf5835815fb`.\n- The completed guarded scan of **24 configured sources / 55 members** and\n  archive `cb77e4b7e2bf7aa6ec2dff5176a862a4ef737c69dfeb6e98d1e0c3055c11ba10`\n  found **zero active recipe-pair findings** in mappings or source/merged\n  semantic identity fields. It scanned 3,808,331 source nodes / 17,710,444\n  source edges and 3,354,496 merged nodes / 17,647,501 merged edges. Report:\n  `data/mim-ship-20260925.QDVfoK/finite-identity-v2-8dc51abd-cb77e4b7-20260927/report.json`,\n  SHA `e262777e6d047125eda9fc63f7729456dd60311fefd81948f57113ad5f5862c2`;\n  complete finding ledger SHA\n  `5acaaa8b33f74b243ac71cf086a78dfa100205b7124cf0311bb9e2a2a2b2b244`.\n- Rejected rows remain in quarantine, not deleted. The accepted candidate\n  audit retained all 2,574 rows in its broader policy-rejection cohort and\n  all 181 rejected-label rows, with zero missing original full rows; these\n  are not recipe-only counts. Audit SHA\n  `8ba12e0af859b4cb2bbb108bffc53c40fa0b4f385a5f9943461d554da5ff275f`,\n  quarantine SHA\n  `2f7b28e592bee9f605884351d1cf23abd748a15e6cb7bc7837e92e5ca0e9909a`.\n- Instructions remain source evidence. The same archive's MediaDive occurrence\n  check passed all **39,879 positions** with complete original source records,\n  plus **8,639 medium–solution links**. Report:\n  `data/mim-ship-20260925.QDVfoK/mediadive-occurrence-v2-8dc51abd-cb77e4b7-20260927.json`,\n  SHA `232873da0c0d85545a1a12fdc7dfdd96edcae1afa44d92d2b8a7e8ca5f601bc1`.\n- Fresh targeted recipe-identity regression: **35 tests passed**. Legitimate\n  parenthesized names and native authority labels remain permitted; no generic\n  parenthesis filter or guessed replacement identity was added.\n- Independent closure review confirmed the original cohort, current installed\n  hashes, full finding ledger, quarantine preservation and occurrence evidence:\n  `data/mim-ship-20260925.QDVfoK/ISSUE1009-INDEPENDENT-CLOSURE-READINESS-20260927.md`,\n  SHA `be3513793ea581ff614f7dec3c21fdfa840043e9fa893ed8e45881d1262f022c`.\n\nThe broader finite scan intentionally remains `REVIEW_REQUIRED` for twenty-eight\nnon-recipe native-metadata findings. Those are not waived or relabeled PASS by\nthis closure. Overall acceptance remains open in #1123; NCIT/Sugar scope and\ninput guards remain tracked by #1180/#1192. This is not public-release approval.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-27T06:57:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1009#issuecomment-5853584102","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1009,"state":"CLOSED","title":"The unified name index carries MediaDive recipe instructions as entity names","url":"https://github.com/Knowledge-Graph-Hub/kg-microbe/issues/1009"}
